# The build context is what `go build ./cmd/webhook` reads, and nothing else. An allowlist, so the
# `COPY . .` layer, and the compile after it, are reused until Go source or the module files
# change, instead of being rebuilt for a docs, workflow or .git change. Add a directory here if the
# webhook starts importing from a new one; the docker job in ci.yaml fails if one is missed.
*
!go.mod
!go.sum
!cmd
!internal

# Inside the allowed directories, files the compiler never reads.
**/*_test.go
**/testdata
